{"slug":"monthly-rotation-across-btc-eth-and-sol","name":"Monthly rotation across BTC, ETH and SOL","status":"rejected","created_at":"2026-11-14T23:38:07.936478Z","version":1,"frozen":true,"implementation":"monthly-rotation","runs":3,"trials":3,"deflated_sharpe":0.0021501880174973342,"asset_class":"crypto","sections":{"hypothesis":"Hypothesis","rationale":"Why the edge should exist","rules":"Rules in plain English","falsification":"What would prove it wrong","parameters":"Parameters and allowed ranges","costs":"Expected turnover against costs"},"notes":[{"version":1,"created_at":"2026-11-14T23:38:07.936478Z","sections":{"hypothesis":"Holding, each month, the two of BTC, ETH and SOL with the best trailing return among those above their 200-day average (cash otherwise) beats holding the same coins at the same average exposure on Sharpe, after costs.","rationale":"Who pays: time-series momentum, documented in crypto (Liu and Tsyvinski 2021) and across asset classes (Moskowitz, Ooi and Pedersen 2012): investors under-react to news, then pile in late, so a coin's past months predict its next. The 200-day filter is absolute momentum (Antonacci's dual momentum): rank first, then require the trend to be up, so a falling market goes to cash. Outside evidence for the ETF version: Rayner Teo's backtest 2006-2025 (+535%, drawdown 22%; Luke's YouTube batch 3 G3) and Faber's moving-average timing (batch 2 A6). Overlap, stated honestly: BTC/ETH weekly rotation (dropped: Sharpe 1.06 vs 1.07) and cross-sectional momentum top 5 (dropped) are close relatives, and trend-vol-target (pursue) already rides BTC's trend. This differs in the monthly horizon (fewer, slower trades), a 12-month ranking and SOL as a third choice. Freezing it is Luke's knowing override of the entry bar if he judges it a variant.","rules":"Daily bars, UTC, spot, long only. At the close of each month's last day: among BTCUSDT, ETHUSDT and SOLUSDT, a coin is eligible with lookback_days of unbroken history and a close above its trend_days average. Rank eligible coins by their lookback_days return; hold the top top_n at 1/top_n each from the next open; unfilled slots are cash. Positions change only at month ends. SOL joins once it has the history (listed 2020-08). Costs from kestrel.toml, 330 USDT (two 165 USDT slots, well above the 5 USDT minimum). Period 2018-01 to 2025-10, before the holdout. Three settings: lookback_days 365, 180 and 90 (the spec's 12, 6 and 3 months), each with trend_days 200, top_n 2.","falsification":"Scored against the large-basket control and against holding BTC and the same coins at the same exposure, as universe strategies are (CLAUDE.md). The full scorecard; the idea fails if no lookback passes every test. Random entry (test 9) is n/a (weights).","parameters":"lookback_days 30-365, trend_days 50-365, top_n 1-3. Three runs: lookback 365, 180, 90 with trend 200 and top 2. The robustness check moves each parameter around the best of the three (about 8 neighbours).","costs":"At most a few changes a month-end, usually none: perhaps 6-15 round trips a year across both slots, about 0.2-0.4% a year in costs. Trials: 3 runs plus about 8 neighbours."},"implementation":"monthly-rotation","frozen_at":"2026-11-14T23:53:47.815459Z","change_reason":null}],"history":[{"status":"idea","at":"2026-11-14T23:38:07.936478Z","reason":"Created"},{"status":"specified","at":"2026-11-14T23:53:47.815491Z","reason":"v1 frozen"},{"status":"backtested","at":"2026-11-14T23:59:16.706780Z","reason":"first run on v1"},{"status":"rejected","at":"2026-11-15T00:24:22.707017Z","reason":"Failed the scorecard (Luke, 2026-11-15). The note failed its scorecard and is rejected, but it is the only YouTube strategy that beat holding BTC over 2018-01 to 2025-10: Sharpe 1.13, 1.25 and 1.26 (365/180/90-day lookbacks) against 0.74. It fails the drawdown limit (-59%), luck (deflated 30-43%) and out of sample: it beat BTC in only 3 of 11 walk-forward windows, almost all of its lead coming from holding ETH and SOL in 2021. No further work without new evidence; a version with a drawdown control would be a new note with new trials."}],"trial_log":[{"id":"20261114-235916-c56926","created_at":"2026-11-14T23:59:16.702150Z","strategy":"monthly-rotation","strategy_kind":"research","style":"weights","engine":"event","params":{"lookback_days":365,"trend_days":200,"top_n":2},"research":{"slug":"monthly-rotation-across-btc-eth-and-sol","version":1},"strategy_name":"BTC/ETH/SOL monthly rotation, top 2 by 365d","symbol":"UNIVERSE","benchmark_symbol":"BTCUSDT","universe_coins":561,"forced_exits":0,"deflated_sharpe":0.0006272053379368092,"deflated_trials":883,"interval":"1d","start":"2018-01","end":"2025-10","scored_from":null,"history_from":null,"initial_cash":"330.0","account_currency":"USDT","used_holdout":false,"config_fingerprint":"7cba2946385d","code":{"commit":"b28bb196f721a16126077966636c81603e99a019","dirty":false},"metrics":{"start":"2018-01-01T00:00:00Z","end":"2025-11-01T00:00:00Z","days":2861,"final_equity":12383.083627114433,"total_return":36.5244958397407,"cagr":0.5879893296465897,"volatility":0.5378273161449698,"sharpe":1.1302807109037625,"sharpe_ci":[0.4257349282400058,1.8348264935675191],"psr":0.9991676016138422,"sortino":1.6849661528262316,"max_drawdown":-0.5881968375462674,"longest_underwater_days":736.0,"skew":-0.06541092313756963,"kurtosis":10.863852393503624,"exposure":0.5586226782651398,"trades":86,"rejections":0,"band_skips":0,"fees":78.89479977748701,"spread_costs":11.8935889389217,"impact_costs":1.5367725594583161,"total_costs":92.32516127586702,"turnover":2.3948879599431785,"few_trades":false,"round_trips":null,"win_rate":null,"avg_win_r":null,"avg_loss_r":null,"expectancy_r":null,"profit_factor":null,"avg_cost_r":null,"risk_capped":null},"benchmark_metrics":{"start":"2018-01-01T00:00:00Z","end":"2025-11-01T00:00:00Z","days":2861,"final_equity":2699.674499192965,"total_return":7.180831815736257,"cagr":0.3075330193144028,"volatility":0.661012596830815